---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
import '~/styles/prose.css'
import { SITE } from '~/config/site'
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Colophon"
  description="How this site is built — typefaces, stack, design references."
  documentStripLeft="DOCUMENT · COLOPHON"
>
  <article class="container page">
    <header class="page-header">
      <p class="kicker mono-chrome">COLOPHON</p>
      <h1 class="page-title">How this site is set</h1>
      <p class="page-lede">
        A brief accounting of the typefaces, technology, and references
        behind the design.
      </p>
    </header>

    <hr class="rule" />

    <div class="prose colophon-body">
      <h2>Typefaces</h2>
      <p>
        Body and display are set in <strong>Newsreader</strong>, a serif by
        <em>Production Type</em> designed for editorial reading on screen, in
        its variable optical-size form. Newsreader is distributed under the
        Open Font Licence.
      </p>
      <p>
        Chrome, marginalia, figure captions, and code are set in
        <strong>IBM Plex Mono</strong>, designed by <em>Bold Monday</em> for
        IBM. Plex Mono is distributed under the Open Font Licence.
      </p>
      <p>
        Fonts are self-hosted as WOFF2 via <a href="https://fontsource.org">Fontsource</a>.
        No external font CDNs are loaded.
      </p>

      <h2>Stack</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Astro</strong> — static site generator with TypeScript in strict mode.</li>
        <li><strong>Vanilla CSS</strong> with custom-property tokens. No framework, no utility classes.</li>
        <li><strong>Notion</strong> as the content authoring environment, queried at build time via the official API.</li>
        <li><strong>Pagefind</strong> for client-side full-text search, indexed at deploy.</li>
        <li><strong>Vercel</strong> for hosting and deploy hooks.</li>
        <li><strong>pnpm</strong> for package management.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Design references</h2>
      <p>
        The visual language draws on several traditions of mid-century
        technical publishing:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>NASA technical-report design from the Apollo era — cream paper, figure numbering, mixed serif and monospace.</li>
        <li>The Paul Rand period at IBM — restrained accent colour, strict grid, the precision of Helvetica-era marks.</li>
        <li>The <em>Bell System Technical Journal</em> — serious serif typography, formal article structure, dense footnotes.</li>
        <li>Massimo Vignelli's grid systems — ruled lines, deliberate hierarchy, no decoration without purpose.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Source</h2>
      <p>
        The repository will be made public alongside the launch of the
        commerce phase. Until then, anything documented in the notes and
        releases here is offered freely for reuse.
      </p>

      <hr />

      <p class="mono-margin colophon-footer">
        Site &copy; {SITE.established} {SITE.title} · Content licensed under
        Creative Commons BY 4.0 unless otherwise stated.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page { padding-block: var(--s-6) var(--s-8); }
  .page-header { max-width: var(--measure); }
  .kicker { color: var(--c-ink-muted); margin-bottom: var(--s-2); }
  .page-title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: var(--t-d1);
    line-height: var(--t-d1-lh);
    font-weight: var(--w-display-light);
    font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 60;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }
  .page-lede {
    margin-top: var(--s-3);
    font-size: var(--t-body-lg);
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--c-ink-muted);
    font-variation-settings: 'opsz' 24;
  }
  .rule { margin-block: var(--s-5); background: var(--c-rule); }
  .colophon-body { max-width: var(--measure); }
  .colophon-footer { color: var(--c-ink-muted); margin-top: var(--s-3); }
</style>
